    },
    {
      "claim": "There is a large gap between operating cash flow (182.9 billion) and free cash flow (16.5 billion). Whatever the precise cause, this scale of gap is consistent with heavy, ongoing capital spending (consistent with the AI infrastructure buildout the company and its peers describe) eating into the cash that would otherwise support buybacks, dividends, or a valuation cushion. If this capex intensity persists or the AI spending does not convert to revenue as fast as hoped, free cash flow could stay compressed even as revenue and operating income look strong.",
